{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"## Reproduction on arm64 macOS, 2026-10-31 (worktree at origin/main 0886e96f03a)\n\n**The 4 files pass on an unmodified tree here:** `29 passed in 268.42s` (`-n 4`). No commit since 2026-10-27 touches `infra/scripts/observability.sh` or these 4 files, so main has not fixed this; the failure is load-dependent.\n\n**The missing `/var/lib/rebar` paths do not cause the timeout.** Every write to them is `... 2>/dev/null || true`. The two stderr lines in the description come from bash reporting the failed `>` redirect before `2>/dev/null` applies; the script continues and exits 0. The 29 passes above ran with `/var/lib/rebar` absent and those same lines on stderr.\n\n**What makes a run slow: the tests reach the host's real Docker daemon, with no time limit.**\n- `mcp_health_9ea3`, `offsets_6a65`, `marker_anchor_8c2f`, `mcp_markers` stub `curl`, `git`, `logger`, `journalctl`, `aws`, but not `docker`. Inside the test environment, `docker` resolves to `/opt/homebrew/bin/docker` (colima): `docker system df` took 6 s, `docker stats --no-stream` 3 s.\n- This host has no `timeout`/`gtimeout`, so the script's `bounded()` falls back to running each probe with no limit (documented intent at the definition, for portable test hosts).\n- One script run: 15.9 s and 16.9 s with real docker; 5.5 s and 5.0 s with `docker` stubbed to `exit 1`. Load average at the time was about 40 on 18 cores.\n\n**Controlled reproduction of the reported failure:** a `docker` stub that runs `exec sleep 75`, driven through the unmodified `_run` from `mcp_health_9ea3`, raised `TimeoutExpired` at 60.0 s with exactly the 2 stderr lines in the description, and left `bash observability.sh` at PPID 1 with its child and the `sleep` (reaped by pid). This shows that a stalled host probe alone yields the reported signature and the orphan leak in the earlier comment. Whether colima was the stalled probe in the 2026-10-27 run has not been measured.\n\n**Isolation gaps are suite-wide, not limited to these 4 files.** The script has 16 `NAME=\"${NAME:-/var/lib/rebar/...}\"` defaults. Every one of the 21 test files that drives `observability.sh` leaves between 4 and 16 of them unset; only 7 of the 21 stub `docker`. The 4 named files leave 10, 10, 8 and 5 unset respectively. Reads also reach `/var/tmp`, `/var/lib/docker`, `/var/log/journal`, `/var/gerrit`, `/etc/...` and `/usr/local/bin/rebar-*-cap.sh`."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793488425461719001,"uuid":"152b6ea6-e18e-4f47-a5fe-637ea6fe76b5"}